Z||000012||Shiner||09-08-2000||12:57 AM||||Homi,<BR> Yes, us car guys know right away what something is, but it's those other people that don't know.  There is a simple explanation.  Every year in Philadelphia (a few hours away from me), somebody swears they saw a cougar (aka mountain cat) in their backyard, right in the middle of the frickin city.  The police NEVER find any cat, and the illeged mountain cat NEVER attacks anybody.  Do you know why?  Some city slickin' assclown (my apology to you city slickin' assclowns here  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ) has probably never seen a coyote or a fox before, and mistook it for a cougar.  My point?  Most people have never seen a real Ferarri, and wouldn't know a GTO from an F-type Jag.  ||||reg||1
Z||000013||jlhuber||09-08-2000||09:01 AM||||for the people who say that a fiero can't be mistaken for a ferarri because the fiero is soo much smaller... some ferarris that i have seen are almost the same size as the fiero.  close enough that from a distance (10-20 feet), they could look identical to someone other than us fieroites.  that is not to say that all of ferarris are, just some of them.  a lot of people i know think that the ferarris and lambos are huge cars.  from what i have personally seen, they are not.  i am not cutting anyone down, i just have to defend my opinion.  afterall, i do live in a free country.  yup, thats my $0.02  ***crawls back under the rock he's been hiding under***<p>[This message has been edited by jlhuber (edited 09-08-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||Monkeyman||09-08-2000||06:47 PM||||I was talking to a customer in my store today.  Here's an excerpt.<P>Customer:  Who owns the purple car?<BR>Me:  That's mine.<BR>Customer:  Nice paint job...(good so far)...on your <I>Toyota</I>.  (oops...now we're in trouble)<BR>Me:  Sorry.  I thought you were talking about my car.  It's the little sports car right there.  (pointed to the Grape Ape)<BR>Customer:  Yeah.  That's the one I was talking about.  That's an MR2, right?<BR>Me:  Ummm...Not even close.  How about a Pontiac Fiero.<BR>Customer:  No.  That's a Toyota MR2.  My brother had one.  Looked just like it.<BR>Me:  Would you care to see the registration?<BR>Customer:  C'mon.  You can't fool me.  I <I>know</I> what an MR2 looks like.<BR>Me:  Excuse me.  I have some paperwork to do.  (never argue with a customer)||||reg||1
